WEBVTT

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.000
We begin now.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.000
All right?

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Before we go into the first Berakha, which is Atachon El Haram Dahar, let me make a few comments, a few notes.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:33.000
As I told you, the Amilah begins with three B'elachot.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Those three B'elachot are in every single Amilah.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Rosh Chodesh, Rosh Hashanah, Yom Kippur, Ne'ilah, Musa, whatever it is, it must begin in the same way.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:51.000
Now, what is the function of this three B'elachot? It's very important.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:01:01.000
We pray to God. What is God? Is it a song? A phonetic song? God? Or Allah? Or Amonai?

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Or Bajabuddin is a phonetic song? What we believe that in order that the prayer to be meaningful, it has to be a definite meaning.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:19.000
The function of the first three Bera'kot is to define what we understand by the term God.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Now, it's not only important to know what is the meaning of the Vedāpāda or a practice,

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.000
but specifically what is the function.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:51.000
Now the function of the first three verapostes is to define what do we mean by the word God.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.000
What does it mean, God, for us?

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:58.000
So we say it, and I don't want to repeat it again.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:04.000
Maghen Abraham, Nehemiah and Ha'er HaKadol.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:13.000
The three basic components of our understanding of God.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:17.000
And there we explained already in detail, I am not going to repeat it.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:22.000
Now after we define what God is for us, then we start making requests to God.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:28.000
And the first request is going to be at Takh-ul-Inn al-Ahmad-A'at. We're going to see in a couple of episodes.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Now, there is a word, or rather two words, of the preceding barakah that I want to, I did not explain, and I should have explained.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:46.000
One of it is, Ozeru Moshiach, and the other is Maget.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:53.000
Melech, Ozer, Mosheah, Umagen. Ozer means that he helps.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:03:03.000
Umagen means that he's a shield. Now, what is the difference between God being Ozer,

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:12.000
Mosheah, Ozer and Mosheah, because they're together, Ozer and Mosheah are together, and Umagen?

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:30.000
There is two ways in which God helps. One is called Ozer. We live in a natural way. We have a problem and somehow, without us being aware, God intervenes.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.000
and a solution appears in front of us.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:38.000
We do it in which God is Ozef,

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:42.000
help us, and in this way Moshe Yah, He saved us.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:46.000
We do it in what appears to be

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:50.000
a natural process. We went to the customer,

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:54.000
the customer bought, everything was alright,

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:58.000
he took the banana with the strike in the truck, we were able to find an alternative

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:03.000
means of transportation for the merchandise. Everything went in a natural process.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:06.000
Or there...

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:12.000
But then there is the concept of mages. And that concept is very interesting, very important

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:21.000
for us to understand how we Jews perceive the doings of the Lord, the path of the Lord,

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:28.000
of the North, the way in which God behaves. Now, let us take a horrible example. An airplane

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:36.460
crashes. And there is a fiancee, not a friend, they all are zombies. They are in the air

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:43.460
plane. What is the situation? What happened? Now, fortunately there are two kinds of sabdikim

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:47.460
There are two kinds of tzaddikim, or righteous persons.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:57.460
One is the normal tzaddik, and God will be Mosheeh, Ozer Mosheeh, helping within the boundaries of nature.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:01.460
But He will not do a miracle for them.

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:07.460
He will be as far as Ozer.

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:12.460
But, Ozer Moshe Yah, yes? Ozer with the purpose of Moshe Yah, yes? Alright?

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:14.460
What is the difference?

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.460
Then there is another situation.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:18.460
And let me give you an example.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:22.460
A horrible example, because that's the only one that comes to my mind.

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:28.460
Suppose, I don't know, you are the president or the general of the Supreme General of the United States of America.

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:30.460
I don't know.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:34.460
And suppose you know, because part of your design,

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:44.460
that a hydrogen bomb is going to explode, I don't know, in Kiev, in Moscow, or in some, I don't know, enemy territory.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:52.460
You know, that's when you're going to throw a bomb. Or your air force or whatever, they're just going to throw a bomb.

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:54.460
Throw a bomb by that place.

00:05:54.460 --> 00:06:03.460
And it happened to be that a good friend of yours was visiting Kiev or Moscow.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:10.460
Now what should you do? The order has to go.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:21.460
And not to tell your friends, pick up the phone and call up this guy and say, get the hell out of that place.

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:35.460
Now, sometimes things like this do happen in the world. There's going to be an earthquake, or a permanent airplane, or whatever it is, an accident.

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:49.460
God is awesome again. What do you mean again? He rings you up and says, don't take this airplane. Get out of that country. Get the hell out of this. He calls you up.

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:55.460
In that way, God is not only a alter umashiach, but He's also one...

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:57.460
Not yet.

00:06:57.460 --> 00:07:00.460
Do you understand now the difference between one and the other?

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:06.460
It happened to me that sometimes God calls us, and we don't answer.

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:10.460
I want to bring a horrible episode in our history.

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:16.460
Very briefly, I believe that God, since 1939, when Hitler came into power,

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:20.460
He was ringing on the phone from the people to get the hell out of Germany.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:24.460
They were all over there, get the hell.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:28.460
The Goitians were saying, Jews we don't want you here.

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:32.460
Out, Juden heraus,

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:36.460
all over, Jews out.

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:40.460
They were phoning, sending telegraphs, you know.

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:44.460
But God is as two functions.

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:47.460
functions. Neh, Adir Moshiach, that's one.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:51.460
And, Mahat.

00:07:52.460 --> 00:07:59.460
Finished the note that I wanted to make. Now let's begin into the first B'el Hacham.

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:08.460
Now, by the very fact that you have this as the first request, already you could see the wisdom of the Hakarei.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:17.460
Before we ask anything to God, we are going to ask Him intelligence.

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:24.460
Because if you have no intelligence, you do not know what to ask.

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:31.460
And not only you do not know what to ask, even if you get a gift from God,

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:36.460
you do not know how to appreciate it, how to recognize it.

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:40.460
So we begin with a statement.

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:45.460
עצה חונן לאדם שטח.

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:53.460
You give, and I explain exactly the meaning of every word, please, and now at the beginning it's going to be a rough explanation.

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:55.460
עצה חונן לאדם שטח.

00:08:55.460 --> 00:09:02.460
You give man wisdom.

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:12.140
In that statement, already you have an entire philosophy. There's something unique about...on

00:09:12.140 --> 00:09:27.740
man. And that is our faculty to reason. Man is a rational animal. An animal, because it

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:33.740
We are all the make up of an animal. We are a mammals. We are all the symptoms of mammals.

00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:40.740
But at the same time we are rational. Now, how does Weasley think about it?

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:47.740
How come that we are rational and not the monkeys, not the giraffes, not the other animals?

00:09:47.740 --> 00:09:54.740
What's his? Now, I don't think what the truth is, I'm just telling you what I believe and what today is in God.

00:09:54.740 --> 00:10:05.740
The goem understand that the faculty of reason is another faculty, just like we have the power of sight, another value.

00:10:05.740 --> 00:10:12.740
Just like we have the power, I don't know, of smelling, and fish do not smell, or many fish do not smell.

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:21.740
In the same thing, there is something biological in us, which give us the faculty of reason.

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:28.740
This is the standard of religion. We began by denying this.

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:32.740
أَلْتَحْ خُنَيْنَ لِأَدَمْدَاهِ

00:10:32.740 --> 00:10:39.740
You give to men wisdom. But the word خُنَيْن in Hebrew is very important.

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:43.740
It comes from the word חِنَّمْ, gratis, free.

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:48.740
It is not an evolution in man, it's something, it's an additional gift on your part.

00:10:48.740 --> 00:10:55.040
is to be, precise in English, an unmerited gift.

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:58.040
It's not something which is intrinsic to us.

00:10:58.040 --> 00:11:04.040
Like it is intrinsic to us the fact that since we are men we have hair.

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:07.040
Or since we are men we have hot blood.

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:10.040
It's not intrinsic in that way.

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:12.040
It's enum.

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:14.040
It's something unmerited.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:28.040
We could have been exactly the same way, with the same type of brains, which is very close to the brain of a monkey, and be without that.

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:37.040
The fact that we are Da'at, for us the Jews, is ponen, hanna.

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:47.040
In other words, it is a free, unmerited, undeserved, non-intrinsic gift to us.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:12:01.040
So here you see one very important notion about man, evolution of man, all this, all Darwin, non-Darwin, I'm not to be bluntly polemical here.

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:05.040
