Atah Honen L'Adam Da'at

00:19:29.780 --> 00:19:31.780
It's another very important thing.

00:19:31.780 --> 00:19:38.780
We say, there's a very important principle, it is said in Mishlech several times.

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:53.780
Rashid of Mahmoud, he had Adonai. The beginning of wisdom is the recognition of God. He has the fear of God.

00:19:53.780 --> 00:20:07.780
What does it mean? Now, there are two distinct ways, one Jewish and the other non-Jewish, to try to acquire wisdom.

00:20:07.780 --> 00:20:32.960
Two different ways. One way is to try to acquire wisdom by looking into nature. You look into nature and by observing nature, you learn from nature the principles, laws, governing, I don't know, mankind, governing the mind.

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:41.960
You look into the future. And so nature eventually, you hope, some of you, to reach God.

00:20:43.960 --> 00:20:50.960
From man, nature, God. That is the good way.

00:20:50.960 --> 00:21:15.960
